x86_64-linux  clang folds these const doubles away and emits no symbol for them, having used their values everywhere they are read and settled the address comparison without loading either object; cxx1 emits each as an ordinary definition. That is a difference about emission rather than naming - the same one static-assert.cpp records, where a const int every reader folds leaves no symbol either. What this case is about, a const floating object read back so that a later one folds, is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
